  "question": {
    "text": "A transmitting antenna at top of a tower has a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, and the height of receiving antenna is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. What is the range of communication for the line of sight (LOS) mode?<br />[use radius of the earth<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>]</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>144</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>57</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The formula of range of the antenna is given by the formula,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></math>., here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius of the earth then,&nbsp;putting the values, the range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>57</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>.</p>"
